---
import catalog from '../content/packs.json';
import { loadPacks } from '../lib/packs';
const packs = loadPacks(catalog);
const guide = 'https://github.com/nuggocto/orifude/blob/shrek/docs/puzzle-authoring.md';
---
<section id="puzzle-packs" class="packs-section wrap" aria-labelledby="packs-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Share a little paper</span><h2 id="packs-title">Make a puzzle pack.</h2></div>
    <p>Write your own folds and patterns in plain-text files. Share them for review, or keep them on your computer. Every pack plays offline.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pack-guide">
    <div>
      <h3>Submit your papers</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Fork <a href="https://github.com/nuggocto/orifude">Orifude on GitHub</a>. Copy the <a href="https://github.com/nuggocto/orifude/tree/shrek/puzzles/example-pack">example pack</a> into <code>community/your-pack-id/1.0.0/</code>.</li>
        <li>Edit the puzzles and <code>pack.toml</code>. Include your name and a license that permits redistribution. Play every puzzle, then run <code>orifude verify PATH</code> and <code>orifude solve PATH</code> on the folder.</li>
        <li>Open a <a href="https://github.com/nuggocto/orifude/compare/shrek...shrek?expand=1&amp;template=puzzle-pack.md">pack pull request</a> from your fork to <code>shrek</code>. Include the command results, play notes, and any source credits.</li>
        <li>Isolated CI runs the validator and solver. A maintainer reviews the puzzles, text, and license before publishing a versioned ZIP and checksum here.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><a href={guide}>Read the pack format and submission guide</a> for a complete example, limits, and update instructions.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Play a shared pack</h3>
      <p>Download a reviewed ZIP and its checksum file. <a href={`${guide}#download-and-install-a-published-pack`}>Check the SHA-256 checksum</a>, then run <code>orifude pack install FILENAME.zip</code>. Open Orifude and choose Puzzle packs.</p>
      <p>The game never downloads content for you. To update a pack, remove its installed version before installing the new ZIP. Your saved progress and keepsakes remain.</p>
      <p>Pack versions are separate from game releases. These packs work with Orifude 1.0.0 or later.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  {packs.length > 0 && <div class="pack-downloads" aria-label="Reviewed puzzle packs">
    {packs.map((pack) => <article class="pack-download">
      <h3>{pack.title} <span class="small-copy">{pack.version}</span></h3>
      <p>{pack.description} {pack.puzzles} puzzles. {pack.authors.join(', ')} · {pack.license}.</p>
      <p class="pack-links"><a href={pack.zipUrl}>Download {pack.title} ZIP</a><a href={pack.checksumUrl}>SHA-256 checksums</a><a href={pack.releaseUrl}>Release and review</a><a href={pack.sourceUrl}>Pack source</a></p>
      <p class="pack-hash small-copy">ZIP SHA-256: <code>{pack.sha256}</code></p>
    </article>)}
  </div>}
</section>
